Andy,

The user's home dir is probably an NFS mounted filesystem and the NFS
rpc.lockd
is not configured on that system.
Do : /usr/sbin/rcmgr set NFSLOCKING 1
and restart NFS.

For doc see:
http://www.tru64unix.compaq.com/docs/base_doc/DOCUMENTATION/V51_HTML/MAN/MAN
2/0021____.HTM

++++++++++++++++
 [ENOLCK]  The request parameter is F_SETLK or F_SETLKW and satisfying the
	    lock or unlock request would exceed the configurable system limit
	    of NLOCK_RECORD.

	    [Tru64 UNIX]   The file is an NFS file, and either the client or
	    server system is not running rpc.lockd, which is the NFS lock
	    manager.
++++++++++++++++

Johan../





