>>>>> "Oisin" == Oisin McGuinness <oisin@smbc-cm.com> writes:

Oisin> Does anyone have experience with getting the Enterprise Virtual Array
Oisin> SAN product from HP/Compaq to work with version 4.0F of the Tru64
Oisin> Operating System?

Oisin> We're thinking about such a SAN product,  but would like to use
Oisin> it with 4.0x systems (in  particular 4.0F, application issues),
Oisin> and the HP StorageWorks SAN design document suggests it may not
Oisin> be "supported"; what I want to know is does it work.....

Tru64 UNIX V4 has ended _standard_ support. Tru64 UNIX V4 only supports
controllers in transparent failover mode (i.e. HSG80). This means that
the operating system is not required to assist in the failover. The
Enterprise Virtual Arrays can only be used in (what the HSG80 would
call) multibus failover mode. Therefore there are good reasons why
this is not supported. 

