Well, detail would take too much time. Basically, a TruCluster is 2 or 
more SYSTEMS working together, interconnected by a cluster interconnect. 
A single ES40 can be a single node cluster, but you lose all the 
advantages of clustering - automatic failover of applications if a node 
fails, l;oad balancing, etc. 

Your best bet would be to contact your local HP office and ask them for 
detailed information on TruClusters. There are several documents on 
this. If you really want to read on your own, go to  
http://h30097.www3.hp.com and on the left side of the page is a link to 
"documentation". Somewhere in there is on-line cluster documentation.


