Hi Ronnie...

I manage a TruCluster with one ES40 and an ES45 running V5.1a, and we
had similar problems.

I take it that both systems are using memory channel cards
point-to-point for their clustering, or are you going via a hub (or
multiple hubs)?

Are you also using AdvFS domains/filesets?

We have a 50/50 split of our users over our cluster, but the
applications that they use, use different file domains and filesets.

We found that we had problems when the cluster was rebooted, and the
first host into the cluster, picked up all of the file systems. This
meant that when the second host came in, all file system access was
being carried out over the memory channel, and was therefore causing
extra loading across both hosts in the cluster.

To be honest, at one point the cluster almost became unusable because
it was sooooooo slow!

I've now written a script to "balance" out the disks to each host, so
that we no longer get such problems.

In essence, it all hinges around the "cfsmgr" command, which can be
used to move file domains from one host to another.

This may not be the root cause of your problem, but it is certainly
worth looking into.

All the best.

Tony A.
(UK)


