I've never heard of this before, but I can think of a couple things 
to try:
1) restart the prpasswdd and NIS on the computer with the problem.
2) Change the problem computer from a NIS slave server to a NIS
   client.  In general, when you are running Enhanced Security, the 
   prpasswd database on the NIS master server and slave servers have 
   to be updated for each login and failed login, so having NIS 
   slave servers just slows everything down.

I also recommend that you update your NIS master server to V5.1A.
This shouldn't have any impact on your immediate problem, but 
there were some Enhanced Security fields that were added between
V4.0f and V5.1A.  If these fields are added to a users prpasswd
entry by one of the other systems the NIS master server should
add them properly, but I'm pretty sure you won't be able to 
manipulate these fields on the NIS master server and it will 
just ignore them.

Ann


