sar is in the systemV environment, depending on your version of Tru64
you may need a license. If you are using a modern (5.1x) version then
you should find the SysV kit on one of the associated product CD's.
As for 'disks' well there are lots of new things to learn, start at
www.tru64.org follow the documentation link then off to Tru64 Online Doc Sets
(http://h30097.www3.hp.com/docs/pub_page/doc_list.html)look for your flavour
of Tru64 and then look for the system administration guide, it talks you
through most of the bits of stuff you will need.

Hope this helps some
Adam




