I've heard of sar and an open source tool I use a lot on tru64 is 
'monitor'.  It allows you to monitor the various subsystems such as CPU, 
memory, disk, swap etc.  I think it was even written by Digital folk 
originally.

If you want to use commands that come with the O/S, I've used iostat for 
disk monitoring and netstat for network traffic etc.  Then there's the 
vanilla 'ps' etc.



